  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Huntington Ingalls has $3.8B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Huntington Ingalls received 75 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $50.7M. Huntington Ingalls obligations are down 9.3% year over year for the current fiscal-year-to-date period. Huntington Ingalls Ship Building and Repairing is the dominant market, accounting for $3.7B of obligations in FY2026 to date. Huntington Ingalls obligations have varied by fiscal year: FY21 totaled $3.6B, FY22 totaled $3B, FY23 totaled $3.2B, FY24 totaled $3.6B, and FY25 totaled $4.2B. Huntington Ingalls also shows smaller FY2026-to-date obligations in Engineering Services at $65.7M, Other Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $51.8M, Power Boiler and Heat Exchanger Manufacturing at $7.5M, and Hardware Manufacturing at $0.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Huntington Ingalls' federal revenue changed over time?",
        "body": "Huntington Ingalls obligations rose and fell across the last six fiscal years, peaking at $4.2B in FY25 and standing at $3.8B in FY26 to date. Huntington Ingalls obligations were $3.6B in FY21, $3B in FY22, $3.2B in FY23, and $3.6B in FY24. Huntington Ingalls obligations are down 9.3% year over year in the current fiscal-year-to-date comparison."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where do Huntington Ingalls' federal obligations concentrate?",
        "body": "Huntington Ingalls obligations concentrate in Ship Building and Repairing at $3.7B for FY2026 to date. Huntington Ingalls also has obligations in Engineering Services at $65.7M, Other Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $51.8M, Power Boiler and Heat Exchanger Manufacturing at $7.5M, and Hardware Manufacturing at $0."
      }
    ]
